Fix ImGui overlay window-content flicker on GL3Plus at high/uncapped frame rates.

OGRE's ImGuiOverlay keeps ONE shared dynamic vertex/index buffer and only
reallocates it when it needs to grow, reusing it across frames otherwise. When
the CPU runs ahead of the GPU (uncapped frame rate, or vsync scanout timing),
the next frame's writeData() overwrites a buffer the GPU is still reading from
the previous frame's draw, so windows drawn later in the frame lose their
geometry -- seen as flicker/blanking of ImGui window content.

Allocate a fresh vertex+index buffer every frame instead. A brand-new buffer
cannot alias the previous frame's in-flight draw, and GL defers the old
buffer's deletion until its draw completes. The buffers are small (tens of KB)
and the driver pools them, so per-frame allocation is cheap.

--- a/Components/Overlay/src/OgreImGuiOverlay.cpp
+++ b/Components/Overlay/src/OgreImGuiOverlay.cpp
@@ -374,17 +374,16 @@ void ImGuiOverlay::ImGUIRenderable::updateVertexData(ImDrawData* draw_data)
 
     VertexBufferBinding* bind = mRenderOp.vertexData->vertexBufferBinding;
 
-    if (bind->getBindings().empty() || bind->getBuffer(0)->getNumVertices() < size_t(draw_data->TotalVtxCount))
-    {
-        bind->setBinding(0, HardwareBufferManager::getSingleton().createVertexBuffer(
-                                sizeof(ImDrawVert), draw_data->TotalVtxCount, HBU_CPU_TO_GPU));
-    }
-    if (!mRenderOp.indexData->indexBuffer ||
-        mRenderOp.indexData->indexBuffer->getNumIndexes() < size_t(draw_data->TotalIdxCount))
-    {
-        mRenderOp.indexData->indexBuffer = HardwareBufferManager::getSingleton().createIndexBuffer(
-            HardwareIndexBuffer::IT_16BIT, draw_data->TotalIdxCount, HBU_CPU_TO_GPU);
-    }
+    // PSX engine patch: allocate a FRESH vertex+index buffer every frame rather
+    // than reusing one across frames. Reuse let the CPU overwrite a buffer the
+    // GPU was still reading from the previous frame's draw (ImGui window content
+    // flicker under GL3Plus at high/uncapped frame rates). A new buffer each
+    // frame cannot alias the in-flight draw; GL defers the old buffer's deletion
+    // until its draw completes.
+    bind->setBinding(0, HardwareBufferManager::getSingleton().createVertexBuffer(
+                            sizeof(ImDrawVert), draw_data->TotalVtxCount, HBU_CPU_TO_GPU));
+    mRenderOp.indexData->indexBuffer = HardwareBufferManager::getSingleton().createIndexBuffer(
+        HardwareIndexBuffer::IT_16BIT, draw_data->TotalIdxCount, HBU_CPU_TO_GPU);
 
     // Copy all vertices
     size_t vtx_offset = 0;
